  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The vapour pressure vs. temperature curve for a solution solvent system is shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e34e911e-7db7-4f31-82b5-1b8776b84421.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 275px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The boiling point of the solvent is _____&deg;C.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "82",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>We know that the temperature at which vapour pressure of a liquid becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;atm. is called the boiling point of the liquid.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e34e911e-7db7-4f31-82b5-1b8776b84421.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 275px;\" /></p><p>From the figure, we can clearly see that Graph I is for pure solvent whereas graph II is for solution. Hence the boiling point of solvent and solution are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>82</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>83</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
